ary":"An industrial-era steam signal remains part of Georgia Tech’s daily soundscape.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech identifies the steam whistle as its oldest recorded tradition and says it signals class changes, touchdowns, home football victories, and the When the Whistle Blows memorial ceremony.","source_url":"https://www.traditions.gatech.edu/whistle.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: The Whistle","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The whistle can be heard outdoors on campus; its weekday pattern follows the class schedule and may change with Institute operations.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-rat-cap-decoration","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Georgia Tech RAT Cap","title":"Write a Semester Onto a Gold Cap","subtitle":"First-year students personalize a Convocation keepsake","notes":"If you receive a RAT cap, add your name, major, hometown, graduation year, and game scores using the documented layout.","short_summary":"A marked-up gold cap becomes a compact record of a student’s first year.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech says first-year students receive RAT caps at Convocation and documents how students traditionally add personal information and football scores to them.","source_url":"https://traditions.gatech.edu/ratcaps.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: Rat Caps","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Cap distribution is associated with first-year Convocation; participation in decorating or wearing one is voluntary.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-t-book-convocation","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Georgia Tech T-Book","title":"Collect the Traditions Handbook","subtitle":"A revived campus guide is distributed to entering students","notes":"Pick up the T-Book through first-year programming, then use its sections on Tech history, songs, spirit, and RAT caps as a reference.","short_summary":"Georgia Tech’s century-old student handbook connects each entering class with campus customs.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech documents that the T-Book originated as a new-student guide, was revived in print in 2008, and is distributed to entering students at Convocation and through first-year programs.","source_url":"https://traditions.gatech.edu/tbook.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: T-Book","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Physical copies are intended for entering students and distributed through Convocation and selected first-year programs; availability may vary.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-mini-500","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Mini 500","title":"Race Tricycles Around a Parking Deck","subtitle":"Homecoming teams combine pedaling, pit work, and engineering","notes":"Watch teams attempt eight laps around Peters Parking Deck while completing required front-wheel rotations with their pit crews.","short_summary":"Georgia Tech turns children’s tricycles into a technical Homecoming team challenge.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech documents the Mini 500 as a Ramblin’ Reck Club tradition held since 1969, with teams racing tricycles for eight laps around Peters Parking Deck and rotating the front wheel three times.","source_url":"https://traditions.gatech.edu/mini500.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: Mini 500","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This is a scheduled Homecoming event; team participation has rules and advance organization, while spectator arrangements vary by year.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-freshman-cake-race","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Freshman Cake Race","title":"Run Up Freshman Hill for Cake","subtitle":"A pre-sunrise first-year race ends with cupcakes","notes":"Eligible first-year students can register for the half-mile Homecoming run; spectators should confirm that year’s early start and route.","short_summary":"A former cross-country tryout survives as a short first-year Homecoming race with baked rewards.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech says the Cake Race began in 1911 and now takes place before sunrise on Homecoming morning as a half-mile first-year race ending atop Freshman Hill, with cupcakes for finishers and cakes for winners.","source_url":"https://www.traditions.gatech.edu/cakerace.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: Freshmen Cake Race","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Participation is intended for first-year students and requires current event instructions; the route and start time should be reconfirmed each Homecoming.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-ramblin-wreck-parade","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Ramblin’ Wreck Parade","title":"Parade Human-Powered Contraptions","subtitle":"Student-built machines join classic cars at Homecoming","notes":"Stand along the announced Homecoming route to see classic cars, fixed bodies, and human-powered contraptions led by the Reck.","short_summary":"An unsafe road race evolved into a campus parade centered on inventive vehicles.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech says students created the Ramblin’ Wreck Parade after the 1929–30 Old Ford Race was deemed unsafe; today its categories include classic cars, fixed bodies, and human-powered contraptions.","source_url":"https://traditions.gatech.edu/reckparade.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: Ramblin’ Wreck Parade","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Attend only on the published Homecoming route and remain in designated spectator areas; timing and street controls vary annually.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-george-p-burdell","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"George P. Burdell","title":"Meet the Alumnus Who Never Existed","subtitle":"A 1927 enrollment prank became a durable campus persona","notes":"Trace Burdell’s fictional biography through Tech history, but leave modern registrations and official records untouched.","short_summary":"Generations of Yellow Jackets have extended the biography of an imaginary graduate.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech documents that student William Edgar Smith created George P. Burdell with a spare enrollment form in 1927 and that later students continued placing the fictional alumnus into campus and public records.","source_url":"https://www.traditions.gatech.edu/gpb.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: George P. Burdell","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Explore the documented story without submitting false registrations, altering systems, or placing the fictional name in official records.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-t-night","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"T-Night","title":"Learn Tech Traditions in One Night","subtitle":"A welcome-week festival and show introduce campus customs","notes":"Check the Week of Welcome calendar for T-Night, then use its booths and stage program to learn traditions and meet student groups.","short_summary":"Georgia Tech packages its customs and student organizations into a first-week festival and show.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech’s 2025 calendar documented T-Night as a free, all-student Traditions Night featuring tradition booths, student-organization showcases, a festival, and an indoor show.","source_url":"https://calendar.gatech.edu/event/2025/08/24/t-night","source_title":"T-Night | Georgia Tech Campus Calendar","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The cited event occurred in 2025; consult the current Week of Welcome calendar before relying on its date, venue, format, or admission details.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-up-with-white-and-gold","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Up With the White and Gold","title":"Answer Red and Black With White and Gold","subtitle":"One of Georgia Tech’s two documented fight songs","notes":"Learn the short fight song from Tech’s traditions page, then listen for the marching band’s arrangement at campus ceremonies and games.","short_summary":"A 1919 song turns Georgia Tech’s colors and rivalry into a compact musical ritual.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech identifies “Up With the White and Gold,” written by Frank Roman and released in 1919, as one of the Institute’s two fight songs honoring its old-gold-and-white colors.","source_url":"https://traditions.gatech.edu/gtsongs.html","source_title":"Georgia Tech Traditions: GT Songs","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The song may be heard at ceremonies and athletics events; event admission requirements depend on the specific performance venue.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["T-Night is supported by a direct 2025 event page; its recurrence, date, format, and free admission must be reconfirmed for later years.","Event routes, eligibility rules, regis